    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61563" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λᾰγώφθαλμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		lit. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hare-eyed</i>: hence,
				<i>unable to close the eye</i>, owing to shortening of the
			upper eyelid, Dem. Ophth. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				7.75
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.681
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				7.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.10
			</span></i>; 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαγόφθαλμος</span>
			:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαγωόφθαλμος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				812.2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ λ.</span> this condition of
			eyes, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.439
			</span></i>.</div>
